<blockquote>
<p>This strikes me as weird for the sake of weird, with the only thing existing beyond that</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Not going to lie, but this version is intended for weird for weirdness sakes.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>being the fact that's yet another thing that seems designed to fuck with the Foundation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is where I disagree. The original version was more true to the &quot;fuck with the Foundation&quot; part, with researchers going nuts over the SCP. Here, it is much toned down and the Foundation find ways to circumnavigate this problem. At the most, with D-class as interviewers, it's not going to do much damage to the Foundation at large.</p>
<blockquote>
