			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2507364">
									

<blockquote>
<p>This is where I disagree. The original version was more true to the &quot;fuck with the Foundation&quot; part, with researchers going nuts over the SCP. Here, it is much toned down and the Foundation find ways to circumnavigate this problem. At the most, with D-class as interviewers, it's not going to do much damage to the Foundation at large.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That's not my problem. My problem is whenever someone writes something like this (and there's quite a few), where the skip displays awareness of the Foundation and is all like &quot;plz contain me lol&quot;, I can't help but wonder how the world as we know it still exists. Since the Foundation is so bad at its job of protecting consensus reality that such things are possible. It's immersion-breaking.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>That's the improvement the SCP made, to do what people believe it could do but it can't in reality.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I have no idea how that's an improvement. There might be a point to that, if it were somehow some sort of commentary on popular misconceptions (though that in itself would be kind of tired), but this is too disjointed and random to be doing anything with that. Honestly, that defense sounds a lot like the &quot;well it's supposed to not make any sense&quot; line that gets trotted out frequently in response to being called out on things that don't make a whole lot of sense in an article.</p>

